---
import { domains } from '../lib/exam-scope';

const examGuide = 'https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-certification/latest/ai-business-strategist-01/ai-business-strategist-01.html';
const certification = 'https://aws.amazon.com/certification/certified-ai-business-strategist/';
const officialPractice = 'https://skillbuilder.aws/learn/NN5MQE4G3M/official-practice-question-set-aws-certified-ai-business-strategist-aibc01--english/9TUSJ7NJ7N';
---
<section class="faq" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
  <h2 id="faq-heading">AWS Certified AI Business Strategist (AIB-C01) FAQ</h2>
  <div class="faq-items">
    <details>
      <summary>What is AWS Certified AI Business Strategist (AIB-C01)?</summary>
      <div class="answer">
        <p>AWS Certified AI Business Strategist is a certification for making business decisions about AI. AIB-C01 is the exam code. It tests how you prioritize AI investments, build a business case, manage risk, and scale successful pilots across an organization. <a href={certification}>AWS certification overview</a></p>
      </div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Who is the AWS Certified AI Business Strategist exam for?</summary>
      <div class="answer">
        <p>The exam is for professionals who evaluate, sponsor, or scale AI initiatives. Typical candidates include product and program managers, business analysts, consultants, and business leaders who work with technical teams. <a href={examGuide}>AWS candidate profile</a></p>
      </div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Do I need coding, hands-on AWS experience, or another certification?</summary>
      <div class="answer">
        <p>AWS requires none of these. It recommends about six months working with or alongside teams adopting AI, plus familiarity with basic AI concepts and what AWS AI services offer at a business level. <a href={certification}>AWS certification prerequisites</a></p>
      </div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What topics are covered on the AIB-C01 exam?</summary>
      <div class="answer">
        <p>The exam covers four domains. These percentages show how AWS weights the scored content.</p>
        <ul>
          {domains.map((domain) => <li>{domain.name} ({domain.weight}%)</li>)}
        </ul>
        <p><a href={examGuide}>Official exam guide</a></p>
      </div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>How long is the AIB-C01 exam, and what is the format?</summary>
      <div class="answer">
        <p>The <a href={examGuide}>AWS exam guide</a> lists 130 minutes. The exam is currently in beta, so the <a href={certification}>AWS certification page</a> lists 170 minutes for the beta. Questions include single-answer multiple choice and multiple response. For multiple-response questions, select every correct option to earn credit.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What is the passing score for AIB-C01?</summary>
      <div class="answer">
        <p>AWS reports scores on a scale of 100 to 1,000. You need an overall scaled score of 700 to pass. <a href={examGuide}>AWS exam scoring</a></p>
      </div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Where can I find free AIB-C01 practice questions?</summary>
      <div class="answer">
        <p><a href="#configure">Start a free practice session</a> on this site to answer original, unofficial questions and see an explanation after each answer. Choose one domain or mix all four. No account is needed. AWS Skill Builder also offers a free <a href={officialPractice}>Official Practice Question Set</a> with 20 questions.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>How should I prepare for the AIB-C01 exam?</summary>
      <div class="answer">
        <p>Start with the <a href={examGuide}>official exam guide</a>. Practice by domain to find gaps, then try a <a href="#exam-config">timed mock exam</a> across all four domains. Review why each correct answer fits the business scenario, especially when several options sound reasonable.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .faq {
    margin-bottom: 72px;
    padding-top: 36px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  h2 {
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
  }
  .faq-items {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--surface);
  }
  details + details {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  summary {
    position: relative;
    padding: 16px 52px 16px 20px;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
  summary::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    right: 22px;
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    border-right: 2px solid var(--muted);
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--muted);
    transform: translateY(-65%) rotate(45deg);
  }
  details[open] > summary::after {
    transform: translateY(-30%) rotate(225deg);
  }
  summary:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--ink);
    outline-offset: -4px;
    border-radius: 12px;
  }
  .answer {
    padding: 0 20px 18px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }
  .answer a {
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  ul {
    margin: 8px 0;
    padding-inline-start: 22px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .faq {
      margin-bottom: 48px;
      padding-top: 28px;
    }
    h2 {
      font-size: 1.375rem;
    }
    summary {
      padding-left: 16px;
    }
    .answer {
      padding-inline: 16px;
    }
  }
</style>
